User Management
TC-UM-01: Add New User
Test Scenario: Verify that an authorized user (Admin/Superadmin) can successfully add a new user.
Steps to Execute:
Log in as an Admin or Superadmin.
Navigate to the User Management page.
Click the "Add New User" button.
Fill in all required fields (Name, Email, Role) with valid details.
Click "Save" or "Submit".
Expected Result: The new user profile is created successfully and appears in the user list with an "Active" status.

TC-UM-02: Edit Existing User Details
Test Scenario: Verify that an existing user's details can be updated.
Steps to Execute:
Navigate to the User Management list.
Select an existing user profile and click "Edit".
Modify the user information (e.g., Name, Phone Number, or Role).
Click "Save Changes".
Expected Result: The user's details are updated successfully, and a notification message confirms: "User updated successfully."

TC-UM-03: Block Active User
Test Scenario: Verify that an Admin or Superadmin can block/deactivate an active user account.
Steps to Execute:
Select a user account with an "Active" status.
Click the "Block" or "Deactivate" button.
Confirm the action in the prompt/dialog box.
Expected Result: The user's status changes from "Active" to "Blocked/Inactive". The user is immediately prevented from logging into the system.

TC-UM-04: Unblock Blocked User
Test Scenario: Verify that a previously blocked user account can be reactivated.
Steps to Execute:
Navigate to the User Management list.
Filter or locate a user marked as "Blocked" or "Inactive".
Click the "Unblock" or "Reactivate" button.
Confirm the action.
Expected Result: The user's status reverts to "Active", and the user can log in to the system again.

TC-UM-05: Approve Pending User Registration
Test Scenario: Verify that an Admin can approve newly registered user accounts.
Steps to Execute:
Navigate to the "Pending Approvals" tab or list.
Select a user account waiting for approval.
Click the "Approve" button.
Expected Result: The account status becomes "Active", and an approval email/notification is sent to the user.

TC-UM-06: Designate User as Admin
Test Scenario: Verify that a regular user's role can be updated to Admin.
Steps to Execute:
Select a regular user account from the user list.
Click "Edit" or "Change Role".
Select "Admin" from the role dropdown options.
Save the changes.
Expected Result: The user's role updates to Admin, and appropriate administrative privileges are granted.

TC-UM-07: Admin Cannot View or Edit Superadmin Profile (Role Access Security)
Test Scenario: Verify role-based authorization restricting Admins from viewing or modifying Superadmin accounts.
Steps to Execute:
Log in using an Admin account.
Navigate to the User Management list.
Search for a Superadmin user profile.
Expected Result:
The Superadmin account is hidden from the list, OR
If displayed, all action buttons (Edit, Delete, View, Change Role) for the Superadmin profile are disabled/hidden.

TC-UM-08: Last Superadmin Guard (Deletion Guard)
Test Scenario: Verify that the system prevents deleting, demoting, or blocking the sole remaining Superadmin.
Steps to Execute:
Log in as a Superadmin.
Ensure there is only one active Superadmin account in the system.
Attempt to delete, demote (change role), or block this last Superadmin account.
Expected Result:
The operation is blocked and an error message appears (e.g., "Action prohibited: Cannot delete, demote, or block the last remaining Superadmin.").

The Superadmin account retains its status and role.
